WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:13.862
Hi, friends. Gani here. This is The Friendly No.

00:00:13.862 --> 00:00:19.723
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:19.723 --> 00:00:23.240
Hands resting on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:26.757
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:26.757 --> 00:00:34.964
There is a small word that does a big job. The word is no. Everybody gets to use it — grown-ups, and you, too.

00:00:34.964 --> 00:00:44.343
A friendly no is short, and warm, and complete. It sounds like this: "No, thank you." Or this: "I don't want to."

00:00:44.343 --> 00:00:54.894
That is the whole thing. A no does not need a pile of reasons. It does not need a string of sorries. One kind sentence is enough.

00:00:54.894 --> 00:00:59.583
And a friendly no is always aimed at the thing — never at the person. Let me show you.

00:00:59.583 --> 00:01:10.134
When you say your no, your words and your body tell the same story. A calm voice. A steady body. The word does the work.

00:01:10.134 --> 00:01:20.685
And hear this part carefully: a no said with a smile is still a no. The word rules — not the face it arrives with.

00:01:20.685 --> 00:01:31.236
Now the other direction. Sometimes you will ask, and the answer you hear will be no. That happens to everyone.

00:01:31.236 --> 00:01:40.615
A no you hear is about the thing you asked for. It is not about you. It is not a rejection of you. The friendship is still standing.

00:01:40.615 --> 00:01:41.787
Saying no kindly, and hearing no kindly — those are the two halves of the same skill.

00:01:41.787 --> 00:01:52.339
Here is the rule that keeps a no friendly: once a no is said, it stays said.

00:01:52.339 --> 00:02:02.890
Nobody persuades. Nobody bargains. Nobody asks five more times hoping the answer changes. The no is a finished sentence.

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:11.096
And when you are the one who hears it, the kind move is simple: "Okay." Then everyone goes on with the day.

00:02:11.096 --> 00:02:12.268
A no is never the end of a friendship. Most days, it is barely the end of a minute.

00:02:12.268 --> 00:02:20.475
Short. Warm. Complete. Your no counts.

00:02:20.475 --> 00:02:26.337
Shoulders soft. Let your body rest.

00:02:26.337 --> 00:02:31.026
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:02:31.026 --> 00:02:36.888
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:02:36.888 --> 00:02:42.749
You're ready for what's next.
